      "lineNbr": 30,
      "author": {
        "id": 1334530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-30T00:04:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Removing the `None` simplifies the dict type from `dict[str, Optional[str]]` (which usually appears as *Unknown* when inferred) to `dict[str,str]`. It also allows for the Pythonic `if board in GPIO_WP_MAP` conditional check.\n\n```suggestion\nGPIO_WP_MAP: dict[str,str] \u003d {\n    \"bloonchipper\": \"sysbus.gpioPortB.GPIO_WP\",\n    \"dartmonkey\": \"sysbus.gpioPortB.GPIO_WP\",\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 26,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "8e5e4efbc7793b3bdad547c43c2cce6c8569b9ee",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da0f2b2a_cbfc970a",
        "filename": "util/renode_ec_launch.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1334530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-30T00:04:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Match previous scope and shorten later usages?\n\n```suggestion\nGPIO_WP_ENABLE \u003d \"Release\"\nGPIO_WP_DISABLE \u003d \"Press\"\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "8e5e4efbc7793b3bdad547c43c2cce6c8569b9ee",
